==========================================================================
                                  1.

                 P.U.R.P.O.S.E.   &   D.E.S.C.R.I.P.T.I.O.N. 

      The purpose of this tool is simple.   It is an online BBS lister.
There have been a couple of similiar tools for /X for this purpose in the
past but none to my knowledge supported many options besides viewing a
specified country.  We thought this was nice but why not add some nice
functions like online editing of the list so users could update the list
themselves with thier own boards or other bbs's they may have knowledge of
etc.  Of course this could be a drawback as well if a typical moron decided
to add all his favorite local boards etc.. so of course this would be
solved by a simple configurable access level needed to use the edit
functions..  Of course we have thought of this as well as often as BBS's
change status different groups/changed numbers, etc..  All these functions
and more are included in > T-LiST PRo < by S.R.H /X Design.  Read on...
============================================================================
                                  2.
                  F.U.N.C.T.I.O.N.S.  O.F.  T.-.L.I.S.T.

  If you have not allready installed T-LIST please skip this for now and
move down to section 3!!  :))    If you have read on..

    Ok you have completed the simple install T-List Pro!  Now type TLIST
and you will be presented with a nice looking ANSI of T-LIST :) and a menu
with a list of countries you can select to view and a command line below
the countries that looks a little like this line:

Command (#,S,C,E,A,D,?)

 The commands are as follows:

 #:  Type a number that corresponds with the country you wish to view the
bbs on and T-List Pro will show you a list of the country selected!  :)

 S:  Search option.  T-List Pro will ask you for the string you wish to be
searched for.  After you enter your string hit return and it will ask you
if you would like it to search ALL countries.  Hit return or 'y' (default)
and T-List Pro will start the search.  If you want a specific country to be
searched type 'n' and T-List Pro will show you the country enu again and
ask you which country numbers you wish to be searched.

 C: Color On/Off

 E: Edit list.  When this is entered T-List Pro will ask you to give it the
string to search for that you wish to edit.  If it finds a matching text
and the following command line: Edit (F,N,P,G,S,Q,?) [Continue]

                                 F=Flag
                                 N=Name
                                 P=Phone
                                 G=Group
                                 S=Sysop
                                 Q=Quit
                                 ?=Expanded Help Line

---------- F: FLAG
    If the F function is selected from the edit menu as above it
will come up with this prompt:  Edit Flag (C,E,B,O,?) [Continue]
Just select the type of flag to assign to the specifed BBS.
                              C: Clear Flag.
                              E: Mark as a newly edited BBS
                              B: Mark as a Busted BBS.
                              O: Mark as an Offline BBS.

      ---------- N: NAME
          Edit the Name of the BBS.
      ---------- P: PHONE
          Edit the phone number of the BBS.

  NOTE:  When inputing the PHONE NUMBER be sure to add the appropriate
dashes.. ie.... USA would be as follows:  1-###-###-#### :))
*****IMPORTANT*****  Here is an example of what can happen if you do not
do this:   You add a new BBS in Finland and the number is something like
this:  +35867495325 without the hiphens (358-) T-List would read the '35'
before it could see the '8' afterwards and assume this is a Poland BBS
because of the '35' country code of Poland.

      ---------- G:
          Edit the group of the BBS.
      ---------- S:
          Edit the sysop of the BBS.
      ---------- Q:
          Quit T-List Pro edit menu.
      ---------- ?:
          Expanded Help Prompt.

                                    END OF EDIT FUNCTIONS

A: Add a BBS to T-LIST.    T-List Pro will ask you for the needed
information.   Simply follow online instructions.
  NOTE:  When inputing the PHONE NUMBER be sure to add the appropriate
dashes.. ie.... USA would be as follows:  1-###-###-#### :))
*****IMPORTANT*****  Here is an example of what can happen if you do not
do this:   You add a new BBS in Finland and the number is something like
this:  +35867495325 without the hiphens (358-) T-List would read the '35'
before it could see the '8' afterwards and assume this is a Poland BBS
because of the '35' country code of Poland.

D: Delete a BBS from T-LIST.  T-List Pro will ask you for the text to find.
When it finds a given string T-List will verify whether or not you wish the
entry to be deleted.
==========================================================================
                                  3.
                       I.N.S.T.A.L.L.A.T.I.O.N.

    Un-Arc the T-List Pro archive into the drive that you store your bbs
on!  Or manually place the files where they need to go:

         BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/TLIST.INFO       (COMMAND ICON)
         DOORS:SRH/TLIST/SRH-TLIST_PRO.INFO   (CONFIGURABLE ICON)
         DOORS:SRH/TLIST/TLP2                 (T-LIST PRO 2 XIM MODULE)
         DOORS:SRH/TLIST/SRH-TLIST_PRO2.DOC   (DOCS!!)
         DOORS:SRH/TLIST/SRH-TLIST_PRO.GUIDE  (AMIGAGUIDE DOCS!!)

             In addition to these files you will need an issue of S.R.H.'s
T-LIST.TXT (SRH-TL#.TXT) which is released on a monthly basis.  This can
be located anywhere, but will have all adds stripped, so you might want
to use a copy of your original.

****IMPORTANT****
    Please only use issues 10 and higher of the T-List.txt for proper BBS
highlight flagging operations!  
****IMPORTANT****
       The filename for the T-List txt is: SRH-TL#.TXT... the latest issue
as of the release of this version of T-LIST PRO is SRH-TL8.TXT    If you 
can not find a copy of T-LIST.TXT (doubtful) You can call these boards for 
the latest issue:

               Social Dizease  1-307-234-0580  T-LIST WHQ
